@alife-records 1

node vp_1435.VQ_HOUSE_BATH
  t.any.1 Gladly.. can leave the shirt folded out of the water
  t.any.2 Yes.. prefer washing to having dirt pointed out like it's news
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_HOUSE_BED
  t.any.1 Would take it.. can the door to the room stay open?
  t.any.2 Yes.. outer door secure, my room open if you don't mind
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_HOUSE_CHAIR
  t.any.1 Might sit.. don't make it a big occasion
  t.any.2 Thanks.. not looking to claim the whole room
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_HOUSE_CHORES
  t.any.1 Cleaning's something I can do.. Ruth's lemon rag had more rules than most jobs
  t.any.2 Give me the cloth you want used.. learned not to pick one at random
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_HOUSE_LOCKS
  t.any.1 Please check the outer doors.. want those secure, my own room door open
  t.any.2 Could check with you.. not asking you to lock every room I'm in
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_HOUSE_PHONE
  t.any.1 Would try Janice.. not going to guess what we'd hear
  t.any.2 Janice first.. could dial it without looking at a scrap of paper
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_HOUSE_RADIO
  t.any.1 Would listen.. even a score would be a change from warnings
  t.any.2 Try it.. Ruth always wanted news on before work, I wanted anything else
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_HOUSE_WELCOME
  t.any.1 Thank you.. show me where you don't want me wandering
  t.any.2 Inside sounds better.. won't claim I was too proud to ask
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_CARRYING
  t.any.1 Keys, picture of Dad.. Corky's collar, dog died last year
  t.any.2 Corky's buckle wears smooth under my thumb.. collar's from Janice, after her dog died
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_COLD
  t.any.1 Cold.. vest's mostly for looking employed
  t.any.2 Something warmer would be welcome.. dressed for a bar, not this
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_CRAVING
  t.any.1 Thinking about a bet.. even now, stupid as it sounds
  t.any.2 Gambling.. can find a thing to wager on anywhere, which isn't much to boast about
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_HELP
  t.any.1 Can clean, sort, carry what I can lift.. not just stand making jokes
  t.any.2 Know how to keep a room tidy.. tell me what I can touch first
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_HUNGRY
  gate.rule need:hunger>=2
  t.any.1 Could eat.. not fussy enough to deserve a menu
  t.any.2 Hungry.. been thinking about Janice's cooking more than usual
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_HUNGRY.d
  t.any.1 Not looking for food this minute.. worries don't always come with appetite
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_HURT
  t.any.1 Wouldn't mind somebody checking.. can't tell you every mark just by feeling
  t.any.2 Look if you're worried.. would rather be asked than pronounced fit from a doorway
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_PLAN
  t.any.1 Find out where Janice went.. no clever route in my head yet
  t.any.2 Stop somewhere with people, then ask about Richmond.. don't fancy an empty house
  t.any.3 Need to pick the next thing before I start boasting about it
  t.any.4 Nothing settled. You can hear that without taking me for a fool
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_THIRSTY
  gate.rule need:thirst>=2
  t.any.1 Water would do me good.. plain, don't need bar tricks
  t.any.2 Thirsty.. could take water if there's enough
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_THIRSTY.d
  t.any.1 A drink can wait.. not asking for one right now
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_TIRED
  t.any.1 Could rest.. somewhere I don't have to ask to get out
  t.any.2 Tired.. brain won't stop taking another turn at everything
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_TRUST
  gate.rule trust>=30 & flag:starts_told
  t.any.1 Enough to say I haven't got a brother.. brother in the Guard is something I made up.. wanted people thinking I had someone important to call when I was scared.. got Janice, a sister, no brother waiting to come for me
  fx.1 reveal f_guard
  fx.2 set flag:guard_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_TRUST.d
  t.any.1 Would like to.. keep checking the answer in my head
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_TRUST.d2
  t.any.1 Some trust.. doesn't mean I can say everything straight off
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_WANT
  t.any.1 Outer doors checked.. room to leave my own inner door open
  t.any.2 Want to know strangers can't just walk in.. don't want locking up myself with them outside
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_NOW_WASH
  t.any.1 Would wash.. hate a collar going stiff with dirt
  t.any.2 Yes.. clean shirt would be a welcome ordinary problem
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_OFFER_BLANKET
  t.any.1 Will take it.. better use than looking proud without one
  t.any.2 Thanks for offering.. not too tidy to need warmth
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_OFFER_DRINK
  t.any.1 Water please.. take a turn being served instead
  t.any.2 Water's fine.. know enough about drinks not to need a fancy one
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_OFFER_FOOD
  t.any.1 Could take food.. no jokes about the cooking before I know it
  t.any.2 Kind of you.. don't need anything dressed up for me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_BOSS
  t.any.1 Ruth Payne.. wanted a clean rag and an answer, not the other way round
  t.any.2 Dad first.. Ruth afterward.. both could hear me wasting time from another room
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_CHILDHOOD
  t.any.1 Richmond.. May around most holidays, making me race for things she already wanted
  t.any.2 Dad's shop had a bell on the door.. used to ring it just to hear him answer
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_DAYONE
  t.any.1 At Ruth's bar.. somebody wanted the news louder and everyone stopped ordering
  t.any.2 Working.. Ruth kept wiping the same dry place while the warnings came on
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_FAMILY
  t.any.1 Janice my sister, Dad Rex.. no recent word from either
  t.any.2 Janice is five years older.. cousin May too, if you're counting people who'd complain I left them out
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_FIRSTJOB
  t.any.1 With Dad selling hardware.. thought knowing the tools was enough
  t.any.2 Worked with Rex.. had me counting screws till I stopped acting like the owner's boy
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_HARDEST
  gate.rule trust>=75 & alone & flag:cash_told & imin>=60
  t.any.1 Being shut in.. Dr Nessel told me in ninety it was panic attacks, those spells behind closed doors.. haven't told Janice the diagnosis.. can't bear her knowing how badly a shut door scares me.. want the outside secured, not my own way out blocked
  fx.1 reveal f_spells
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_HARDEST.d
  t.any.1 Losing the store.. wasn't good at watching Dad try not to ask about it
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_HARDEST.d2
  t.any.1 Some things I can't turn into a joke for you
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_HARDEST.d3
  t.any.1 No more digging for the worst bit.. not yet
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_HOBBY
  t.any.1 Bowling.. got a decent score on lane six once, kept the card like I'd won a title
  t.any.2 Bowled for fun till May offered a bet.. then couldn't leave it alone
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_HOUSE
  t.any.1 Rented place in Richmond.. liked keeping my own rooms tidy
  t.any.2 Small rented house.. left the bedroom door open even when I was alone
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_LOVE
  t.any.1 No wife.. went out with Edna from the alley in ninety, didn't last
  t.any.2 Edna.. liked bowling better than she liked me, said I couldn't accuse her of hiding it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_PARENTS
  t.any.1 Rex and Dot.. Dad worked hardware, Mom could make him stop talking prices at supper
  t.any.2 Dot hated bets at the table.. May found that very inconvenient
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_PHOTO
  t.any.1 Dad outside my store.. before it closed, before the sign came down
  t.any.2 Rex in the doorway.. looks like he expects someone to buy the whole place
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_REGRET
  gate.rule trust>=45 & alone & flag:guard_told
  t.any.1 Lake reunion in ninety-one.. May bet she could hit the lodge window with a stone, broke it.. paid for the repair, told the family a branch did it.. kept them off May.. she thought it was funny, I didn't
  fx.1 reveal f_lake
  fx.2 set flag:lake_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d
  t.any.1 Letting May turn everything into a bet.. could have said no more often
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d2
  t.any.1 A family day that cost me more than I wanted to explain
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d3
  t.any.1 Leave the family story alone for now
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL
  t.any.1 Richmond.. finished in eighty-three, went straight to Dad's work
  t.any.2 High school.. got tired of hearing how much I could do if I applied myself
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_SIBLING
  t.any.1 Janice.. older sister, not travelling with me
  t.any.2 Sister Janice.. gave me Corky's collar after he died, ninety-two.. knows I liked that dog
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_TRAVEL
  t.any.1 Nevada with May in ninety-two.. slot machines, cheap room, came back with a comb
  t.any.2 Family reunion by a lake in ninety-one.. rest of my travelling was usually to see somebody
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_TROUBLE
  gate.rule trust>=60 & alone & flag:lake_told
  t.any.1 In ninety-one I used Ruth's spare key after closing.. took eighty dollars from the bar tin to gamble.. she thought a stranger had got in, I agreed.. never found out it was me.. still got the damn key
  fx.1 reveal f_cash
  fx.2 set flag:cash_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_TROUBLE.d
  t.any.1 Store failed.. didn't come out of it feeling respectable
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_TROUBLE.d2
  t.any.1 Some old trouble.. not a story for everybody
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_TROUBLE.d3
  t.any.1 No.. I'm not making this easier by making it public
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_WORK
  gate.rule trust>=15
  t.any.1 Bartender since ninety.. had a store before it went bankrupt in eighty-nine.. tried again that year, ninety, ninety-one.. three starts, never got a lease, none opened.. told Dad one bad year.. sounded cheaper saying one
  fx.1 reveal f_starts
  fx.2 set flag:starts_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_WORK.d
  t.any.1 Bartender for Ruth Payne.. had a shop before, didn't keep it
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_PAST_WORK.d2
  t.any.1 Worked the bar.. store was a different part of my life
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_AGE
  t.any.1 Twenty-eight.. February sixty-five
  t.any.2 Twenty-eight.. Janice says I ought to have improved by now
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_DISLIKES
  t.any.1 A door being shut without anybody asking who's inside
  t.any.2 Somebody licking a finger before they count money.. hated that at the shop
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_FEAR
  t.any.1 Being shut in.. secure the outside, leave me a way through the inside
  t.any.2 Closed doors when somebody else has the key.. don't laugh at that one
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_FOOD
  t.any.1 Janice's pork chops.. she wants compliments before you've swallowed
  t.any.2 Onion rings from the alley.. May counted them when we shared, like I'd steal one
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_FROM
  t.any.1 Richmond.. worked a bar there
  t.any.2 Richmond born.. left the town, haven't stopped thinking about it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_HABIT
  t.any.1 Corky's buckle.. thumb works it even though there's no dog attached
  t.any.2 Smoothing my cuffs.. used to check for a spill before I could see it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_HOPE
  t.any.1 Janice somewhere bossing somebody about food.. that's my hope
  t.any.2 Ruth finding a way to keep busy.. never good at waiting without work
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_HOWARE
  t.lo.1 Dewayne.. can joke or answer, might manage both
  t.lo.2 Wound up.. no, don't try winding me the other way
  t.mid.1 Want something ordinary to happen.. can't seem to arrange it
  t.mid.2 Keep thinking of work.. Ruth would find something for me to wipe
  t.mid.3 Could put a good face on it. Don't think either of us ordered that
  t.mid.4 I'd rather you asked once than kept buying the same answer
  t.mid.5 Better talking without having to keep the whole place cheerful
  t.hi.1 Still jumpy.. knowing you doesn't turn me into a different fellow
  t.hi.2 Could be in a better mood.. could stop apologising for that too
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_JOKE
  t.any.1 Told May I'd bowl a perfect game.. she asked if I meant before or after she died
  t.any.2 Dad called my shop a family business.. nobody bought enough to disturb that arrangement
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_LIKES
  t.any.1 Bowling.. loud enough nobody hears a bad mood arrive
  t.any.2 Fresh shirt folded right.. yes, bar work taught me something besides pouring
  t.any.3 A familiar little routine with nobody making a grand occasion out of it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_LUCK
  t.any.1 Know how to waste money asking it to turn.. slot machines in Nevada, ninety-two
  t.any.2 Lucky at bowling till May turns up.. then suddenly we're playing for something
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_MUSIC
  t.any.1 Fast country.. enough slow songs came out of the jukebox already
  t.any.2 Ruth liked the same three songs.. rather hear anything I haven't heard her hum
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_NAME
  t.any.1 Dewayne Boggs.. one word, not two
  t.any.2 Boggs.. Dewayne unless I've done something worth a full name
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_NERVOUS
  t.any.1 Yes.. not a trick question today
  t.any.2 Been trying to look like I have a reason to stand still.. nervous, yes
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_QUIET
  t.any.1 Could use quiet.. don't need it to be a silence contest
  t.any.2 Fine.. if I start talking, can tell me to stop without a ceremony
  t.any.3 Yes. Not every gap needs somebody talking over it
  t.any.4 Stay if you like. I'm not clearing the place, just shutting up a minute
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_SLEEP
  t.any.1 Prefer the door to my room open.. don't mind a locked outer door
  t.any.2 Hard to settle if I can't get out without asking.. been that way a while
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_SPORTS
  t.any.1 Don't follow ball.. bowling, lane six if I get a choice.. lamp on the other side used to blind me
  t.any.2 No team I pull for.. bowled with May.. did better when she stopped predicting my score
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_STORY
  t.mid.1 Ruth's lemon rag had its own peg.. used it on the floor once, she made me buy a new rag before my shift.. said she didn't sell floor-flavoured drinks.. I thought she was joking till she handed me my coat
  t.hi.1 Corky would wait by my shop at closing.. didn't want me, wanted the paper bag Janice sent supper in.. once I went out empty-handed and he stayed by the door.. thought the better version of me was still inside
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_TALK_WEATHER
  t.any.1 Rain used to bring people into Ruth's.. bad weather paid better than sunshine
  t.any.2 Would take a dry walk.. shoes don't need another drink
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_WORLD_GUARD
  gate.rule !flag:guard_told
  t.any.1 Haven't spoken to any soldiers.. my brother's in the Guard, might know more if I could reach him
  t.any.2 No soldiers close enough to ask.. got a brother in the Guard, haven't heard from him
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_WORLD_GUARD.a2
  gate.rule flag:guard_told
  t.any.1 Haven't spoken to any soldiers.. and no brother in the Guard, that was my lie
  t.any.2 No useful word from soldiers.. shouldn't have invented one in my own family
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_WORLD_HOSPITAL
  t.any.1 Don't know whether they're taking people.. would trust a doctor over my guesses
  t.any.2 No hospital news I can use.. Dr Nessel was in Richmond last I knew, not a report of him now
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_WORLD_NEWS
  t.any.1 Heard warnings at work in Richmond.. nobody I know has sent word since
  t.any.2 News came through Ruth's radio.. can't tell you who was right among the people arguing over it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_WORLD_PLANS
  t.any.1 Check the outer doors first.. easier thinking once that question's answered
  t.any.2 I'd find somebody with real news of family.. less interested in the grand plan
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_WORLD_ROAD
  t.any.1 Walked from the Richmond side.. didn't find out what a car could get through
  t.any.2 Got here, that's the part I know.. wouldn't make a bet on the road now
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.VQ_WORLD_WATER
  t.any.1 Don't know which water is safe.. would ask someone who checks it, not someone who pours drinks
  t.any.2 No reliable source to point you to.. bar work doesn't tell me what the pipes are doing now
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1435.leave.angry
  t.any.1 Rather go than keep at this
  t.any.2 Enough.. I'm leaving, you can like that or not
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1435.leave.plain
  t.any.1 Got my things.. won't make you listen to another closing speech
  t.any.2 Dewayne Boggs.. hope next time there's less to worry about
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1435.react.gave_blanket
  gate.rule gave:blanket
  t.any.1 Blanket's welcome.. I'll manage the corners
  t.any.2 Thank you.. can stop pretending a vest is proper outdoor wear
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1435.react.gave_clothes
  gate.rule gave:clothes
  t.any.1 Thanks.. glad to have the clothes without having to charm them out of somebody
  t.any.2 Appreciate that.. won't waste your patience complaining about style
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1435.react.gave_food
  gate.rule gave:food
  t.any.1 Food's appreciated.. no, not going to rate it like a judge
  t.any.2 Thanks.. Janice would approve of you remembering people need feeding
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1435.react.gave_water
  gate.rule gave:water
  t.any.1 Thanks for the water.. good to be on this side of the giving
  t.any.2 Appreciate it.. no little speech required from either of us
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1435.react.insult
  t.any.1 That's enough of that SHIT
  t.any.2 Could save us both the bother and shut up
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1435.react.refused
  t.any.1 Heard the no.. don't need a bigger one
  t.any.2 All right.. would have liked yes, still know what you said
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1435.react.sorry
  t.any.1 All right.. apology accepted, let it stay accepted
  t.any.2 Heard you.. don't need to keep polishing the sorry
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1435.react.thanks
  t.any.1 Welcome.. don't make me blush, ruins the face
  t.any.2 Glad to help.. had enough practice looking busy
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1435.react.threat
  t.any.1 Wait.. don't want to find out how serious you are
  t.any.2 Can leave.. no need to make me afraid of you as well
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1435.return.arrive
  gate.rule visits>=1
  t.any.1 Boggs again.. kept Corky's collar, couldn't leave that
  t.any.2 Dewayne.. hope there's room for one familiar nuisance
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1435.return.gave_food
  gate.rule visits>=1 & gaveever:food
  t.any.1 Remember being given food here.. glad you did it
  t.any.2 Your food wasn't forgotten.. even with my head making room for every worry
  tag.1 kind:return
end
